<p>I'm afraid it's -1 from me.</p>
<p>I don't think this fits with the Foundation's conservative/cautious ethos (secure, contain, protect). My understanding of Thaumiel is that while half the anomalies on the site could conceivably be weaponised, it is extremely risky to do so. Thaumiel should be reserved for objects the Foundation can't afford to ignore.</p>
<p>Aside from personal interpretations of Foundation philosophy, I don't find the romance of Addendum 4375.8 to be particularly natural or believable.</p>

